    dict(key='09-act-2-figure', kind='figure', title='29 alerts from four queries: true in green, false in amber',
         body='first_queries',
         narration='Second demo: a first version of each rule, as a query. [[slnc 400]] Each bar is one query, and its alerts. [[slnc 300]] Green is a true alert, amber a false one. [[slnc 600]] Brute force at three: one true, two false. [[slnc 300]] Spraying: one, true. [[slnc 300]] Privilege change: one true, one false. [[slnc 600]] And success after failures at one: twenty three alerts, twenty one of them false. [[slnc 300]] Its query groups logins by address, in one-hour buckets, and keeps a bucket with at least one failure and at least one success. [[slnc 300]] It cannot say that the success came after the failures. [[slnc 300]] So every typing mistake, followed by a good login in the same hour, is an alert. [[slnc 600]] Twenty nine alerts, twenty four false. [[slnc 300]] And impossible travel is not here at all: no query can say it.'),
