    dict(key='23-costs', kind='bullets', title='What It Costs',
         body=['Every rule needs the right field mapping', 'Fixed time buckets have edges', 'Thresholds are tuned to one kind of day', 'A query cannot remember the last event', 'Monitors in a console go unreviewed'],
         narration="Nothing is free. [[slnc 400]] Here is what it costs. [[slnc 500]] Every rule needs a field mapping that lets it group by what it means. [[slnc 500]] Fixed time buckets have edges, and an attack that crosses one is split in half. [[slnc 500]] Thresholds are tuned to one kind of day. [[slnc 500]] A query cannot remember a person's previous event. [[slnc 300]] And a monitor clicked together in a console is configuration that nobody reviews."),
